INSERT INTO `ha_term_relationships` (`object_id`,`term_taxonomy_id`,`term_order`) SELECT @translation_id,tt.term_taxonomy_id,0 FROM `ha_term_taxonomy` tt JOIN `ha_terms` t ON t.term_id=tt.term_id WHERE @translation_id IS NOT NULL AND tt.taxonomy='category' AND t.slug='iraq' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM `ha_term_relationships` r WHERE r.object_id=@translation_id AND r.term_taxonomy_id=tt.term_taxonomy_id) LIMIT 1;
INSERT INTO `ha_posts` (`post_author`,`post_date`,`post_date_gmt`,`post_content`,`post_title`,`post_excerpt`,`post_status`,`comment_status`,`ping_status`,`post_name`,`post_modified`,`post_modified_gmt`,`post_parent`,`guid`,`menu_order`,`post_type`,`post_mime_type`,`comment_count`) SELECT 1,NOW(),UTC_TIMESTAMP(),'<h2>Introduction to the Importance of Selecting the Right Pipe in Irrigation Systems</h2>\n<p>Selecting the appropriate irrigation equipment is one of the main challenges for farmers seeking to optimize water consumption and increase farm efficiency. Among the various options, <strong>160 mm threaded pipe</strong> has established a prominent role in drip and strip irrigation systems due to its optimal balance of diameter, pressure resistance, and relative cost. Many farmers are still comparing whether this size from specific brands offers any advantages over other brands. In this article, we analyze the technical and practical aspects of these pipes without making unsubstantiated claims regarding prices or local dealerships, so that you can make an informed decision.</p>\n\n<h2>Technical Features of 160 mm Threaded Pipe</h2>\n<p>To better understand the benefits of this pipe, we must first examine its structure. Threaded pipes are typically manufactured from polyethylene (PE) or polypropylene (PP) of varying grades. A 160 mm diameter is ideal for secondary transfer lines in medium-to-large farms, as it controls pressure drop at long distances. Specifically, the use of high-density materials (HDPE) in constructing these pipes plays a vital role in maintaining pressure consistency in long main lines.</p>\n<ul>\n    <li><strong>Material Composition:</strong> The use of high-density polymers provides the pipe with greater resistance to water flow pressure. Additionally, chemical resistance to high-salinity water is another key advantage of this pipe material, as it reduces internal corrosion.</li>\n    <li><strong>UV Resistance:</strong> One of the most significant weaknesses of minor brands is the lack of UV-resistant additives. High-quality pipes possess chemical stability against sunlight, which extends their useful life in open fields. In contrast, pipes lacking this protection become dry and cracked after the spring and summer seasons.</li>\n    <li><strong>Flexibility:</strong> A 160-millimeter pipe must have the ability to bend properly to be installed along farm pathways without kinking or breaking. This feature is particularly important in sloped fields, as it facilitates easier layout arrangement.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>It is crucial to note that in drip irrigation systems, the pressure applied to the main pipe must not cause deformation of the emitters or connected lines. Therefore, choosing a brand with higher dimensional stability prevents leaks at the joints. This is directly related to irrigation accuracy and uniform plant growth across different rows.</p>\n\n<h2>Comparison of 160 mm Ribbed Pipes with Competing Brands</h2>\n<p>Comparing brands without focusing on specific trademarks, but rather on technical features, is a sensible purchasing method. In this section, we examine the key criteria for comparing 160-millimeter pipes with alternative brands. Farmers should understand that subtle technical differences can drastically alter the total system costs in the long term.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/مقایسه-لوله-نخدار-160-میلیمتر-با-سایر-برندها-تصویر-شاخص.webp" alt="مقایسه لوله نخدار 160 میلیمتر با سایر برندها - تصویر 1"/><figcaption>product comparison brand features 160 mm ribbed pipe</figcaption></figure>\n\n<ol>\n    <li><strong>Wall thickness comparison:</strong> Many lower-priced brands use thinner wall thicknesses (e.g., higher SDR). High-quality pipes with lower SDR values (e.g., 11 or 17, depending on the pressure class) have thicker walls, meaning greater resistance to sudden network pressures. This thickness is critical when opening main valves.</li>\n    <li><strong>Fittings and integrity:</strong> In quality brands, pipes are produced continuously with uniform quality. In lower-tier brands, quality inconsistencies may be observed along the 100-meter length, which increases the risk of rupture. Polymer integrity guarantees no leaks from weld seams or connectors.</li>\n    <li><strong>Filter compatibility:</strong> A 160 mm pipe with a higher freezing and opening temperature offers better compatibility with the pressure of modular filters. This point is important in <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/types-irrigation-tapes-performance/">evaluating the performance of various drip irrigation tape types</a> as well, because pressure drop in the main line directly affects the performance of drip lines and must be calculated precisely.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>One subtle difference is the presence of chemical additives to prevent biofilm growth inside the pipe. Advanced brands utilize chemical anti-bacterial agents or non-wetting structures on the internal surface, a feature less common in generic pipes. The presence of these coatings also increases the lifespan of filters and makes cleaning easier.</p>\n\n<h2>Practical points for the installation and use of 160 mm pipes</h2>\n<p>Proper use of 160 mm threaded pipes is not just about choosing a good brand; how it is installed and maintained during its useful life is crucial. Below is a list of key tips for farmers that can prevent damage from incorrect installation:</p>\n<ul>\n    <li><strong>Cutting and joining:</strong> When cutting 160 mm pipes, use specialized sharp tools to ensure that the cut edges do not damage the connecting collars. The use of pressed or flanged connections suitable for this size is mandatory and must be performed with utmost care.</li>\n    <li><strong>Permitted working pressure:</strong> Never allow the internal pipe pressure to exceed the limit specified on the pipe body. Excessive pressure causes joints to loosen over time, leading to significant water leakage.</li>\n    <li><strong>Shutting down the system:</strong> At the end of every irrigation session, ensure all air is drained from the lines. Air in 160mm pipes in cold weather can cause freezing and pipe rupture. Proper drainage extends the system\'s lifespan for years.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Additionally, pay attention to <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/drip-tape-maintenance-costs/">tip-line maintenance costs</a> and distribution lines, which are part of your irrigation system\'s overall economics. A high-quality, leak-free pipe significantly reduces long-term repair costs and water loss, increasing your farm\'s economic efficiency.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/مقایسه-لوله-نخدار-160-میلیمتر-با-سایر-برندها-کاربرد-عملی.webp" alt="مقایسه لوله نخدار 160 میلیمتر با سایر برندها - تصویر 2"/><figcaption>product comparison brand features 160mm threaded pipe</figcaption></figure>\n\n<h2>Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)</h2>\n<p><strong>Question 1: Is a 160mm pipe suitable for all farms?</strong><br>Answer: Not necessarily. For small farms with low pressure, smaller diameter pipes like 90mm or 110mm may be sufficient and more cost-effective. However, for farms that need to move high water volumes over longer distances, 160mm is a better choice, preventing excess pressure drop.</p>\n<p><strong>Question 2: What is the difference between ribbed and smooth 160 mm pipes?</strong><br>Answer: Ribbed pipes (with external threading) are often used for better identification in the soil or near drip lines, but hydraulically, smooth pipes of good quality perform equally well. The choice should be based on the farm\'s technical needs, not just visual appearance.</p>\n<p><strong>Question 3: How can I prevent early pipe failure?</strong><br>Answer: Regular filter cleaning, preventing mud and debris from entering the pipes, and avoiding excessive pressure beyond the allowable limit. Additionally, inspect cylinder connections for leaks, and perform these checks seasonally.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/مقایسه-لوله-نخدار-160-میلیمتر-با-سایر-برندها-جزئیات-فنی.webp" alt="مقایسه لوله نخدار 160 میلیمتر با سایر برندها - تصویر 3"/><figcaption>product comparison brand features ribbed 160 mm pipe</figcaption></figure>\n\n<h2>Summary and Final Recommendations</h2>\n<p>Ultimately, selecting <strong>ribbed 160 mm pipe</strong> This is a long-term investment. Reputable brands, despite a slightly higher initial cost, offer better economic returns due to improved durability, reduced water loss, and lower maintenance costs in subsequent years. When purchasing, pay attention to polymer quality certifications, wall thickness, and UV resistance. The correct combination of this pipe with the systems <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/%d9%85%d8%b4%d8%ae%d8%b5%d8%a7%d8%aa-%d9%81%d9%86%db%8c-%d9%86%d9%88%d8%a7%d8%b1-%d8%aa%db%8c%d9%be-%d8%a2%d8%a8%db%8c%d8%a7%d8%b1%db%8c/">Technical specifications of drip tape</a> can provide the final optimization for your farm.</p>\n\n<p>In agriculture, water management means cost management. By making smart equipment choices, you can ensure the efficiency of your irrigation system. If you need more guidance on determining drip tape irrigation points, you can refer to the guide on <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/how-to-determine-tape-irrigation-points/">Determining Drip Tape Irrigation Points</a> to implement the 160 millimeter pipe layout in your farm in the best possible way.</p>','160mm Ribbed Pipe vs. Other Brands: Selection Guide for Drip and Tefrip Irrigation','This comprehensive article examines the 160 mm threaded pipe from the perspectives of resistance, service life, and compatibility with drip line systems, and compares it with other brands to help farmers make the best investment decisions.','publish','closed','closed','160mm-ribbed-pipe-technical-comparison-drip-teflip-guide',NOW(),UTC_TIMESTAMP(),0,'',0,'post','',0 WHERE @source_post_id IS NOT NULL AND @translation_id IS NULL AND @slug_conflict IS NULL;
